From e96e57898379bc7417c2478079390c165cbee7c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:54:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Audio] The speakers row says what is accepted, by
 which device, and that the speakers it has are not said

The Audio page of the player information showed "Speakers: 9.1.6 (LG TV
SSCR2); the receiver renders the objects there, heights included" on a
PC connected through a TCL Q85H Pro sound bar to an LG C5 TV. It read as
the user's speakers, a 7.1.4 bar, and as the TV's. None of it was so:

- The EDID that the PC reads is the bar's own. Its HDMI vendor block
  gives the physical address 2.2.0.0, two levels below the TV: a
  repeater sits between the PC and the display, and gives the PC the
  display's name and picture with its own sound blocks. The same blocks
  come from the TV when the PC is on the TV and the bar on its eARC
  (4.0.0.0), and there they may be the TV's own or what it forwards; the
  TV with its own speakers declares none.
- A speaker allocation is what a device accepts, not the speakers it
  has; only a Room Configuration or Speaker Location Data Block says
  those, and the bar sends neither.
- Two of its bits are deprecated by CTA-861-H (F16, RLC/RRC, and F33,
  TpLS/TpRS: "must be 0", which libdisplay-info 0.4.0 reads as nothing).
  TpLS/TpRS made two heights of its own, TSL/TSR: 9.1.6 where the bar
  accepts 9.1.4 (and BtFL/BtFR, which the plan does not place).

SpeakerPlan.h:
- the physical address of the HDMI vendor block is read
  (EdidAudio::physicalAddress); DeclarerOf(): depth 2 or more is a
  repeater between this PC and the display, depth 1 the display or the
  device on its eARC/ARC, which the EDID cannot tell apart; without an
  address (DisplayPort, an ELD) the device the EDID names;
- RoomPlaces(): the speakers of the room only from a Room Configuration
  or Speaker Location Data Block, apart from the allocation;
- Declared(): TpLS/TpRS is never placed (DeclaredOffPlan() names it,
  "deprecated"); RLC/RRC places the backs only in the form of CTA-861-D,
  where no surrounds are named (the 7.1 of HDMI's PCM then); where the
  surrounds are named, the backs are BL/BR's alone.

The row now reads, in English first and in Spanish: "accepts up to 9.1.4
(the device between this PC and LG TV SSCR2); it does not say which
speakers it has; the receiver renders the objects there, heights
included"; with the PC on the TV, "(LG TV SSCR2 or the device on its
eARC/ARC)"; where a room block is there, "its speakers: 5.1.2" in place
of the last part (hades.audio.declsrc, declroom, declnoroom; strings
54961 to 54967). kodi.log says the same, with the address. A CEC
adapter could name the audio system, but NVIDIA has none: no name is
guessed. Worked out where the page is published, never per frame.

The row takes up to six lines in the worst case that the panel can show
(a repeater, no room block, objects not declared, in Spanish): it moves
from the column of the output, which had no room left, to the end of
the left column of the Audio page, which has it (skin_check.py: 564 of
564 px). An ELD gives no physical address: its note ("ELD only: no
heights") goes with the device it names alone.
